%% Peak day (27 Apr): day-ahead plan, approval, offers, then the day itself.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C10 as Connectors (C10)
    participant C5 as Forecast (C5)
    participant C6 as Network model (C6)
    participant C7 as Battery orchestrator (C7)
    participant C8 as DR engine (C8)
    participant OP as Operator (console)
    participant HH as Households / devices
    participant BAT as Battery blocks (C2)
    participant C12 as Settlement (C12)
    C10->>C5: D-1 19:30 weather forecast, day-late meter history
    C5->>C6: P10/P50/P90 net load per phase, 96 intervals
    C6->>C7: forecast violations + safe charge/discharge limits
    C7->>C7: peak-shave plan: fill midday trough, flatten evening peak
    C6->>C8: residual kW above rating after battery, event window
    C8->>C8: stress day? pick 2-h window, LinUCB chooses offer per home
    C7->>OP: draft plan + DR plan (with reasons)
    OP->>C7: approve (D-1 23:30)
    C8->>HH: SMS offers (₹0/25/50/100) · pump schedules · AC event notice
    Note over HH,BAT: Day D
    HH->>HH: enrolled pumps run at ~10:45 on solar surplus
    BAT->>BAT: charge midday (rooftop export first)
    loop every 15 min, 16:30–23:30
        C7->>BAT: re-solve shave level from busbar CT + forecast, setpoint
    end
    HH->>HH: AC event: controllers cycle ACs to 40% for 2 h
    Note over C12: D+1 morning, meter data arrives
    C12->>C12: IPMVP baselines, verify kWh, holdout check
    C12->>HH: DR payments first, then pooled rewards (≤ 20% of revenue)
